title: Definition 4
---
order: 4
---
short_label: X.Def.II.4
---
statement: Again, if the square on the greater term is greater than the square on the lesser by the square on a straight line incommensurable in length with the greater, then, if the greater term is commensurable in length with the rational straight line set out, let the whole be called a <i>fourth binomial</i>;
---
group: defX.II
---
subsection: II
---
body:

